Join us for Zig Day in Portland on Sunday, October 11th at the McMenamins Broadway Pub.

Whether you are new to Zig or have used it since v0.4, come meet other Zig users,
work on something together, and share what you learn.

[**PLEASE RSVP ON LUMA**](https://luma.com/i7rfzqoa) so that we can appropriately plan
for the number of guests.

What to bring:
* A laptop and/or other hardware
* An idea for something to work on that is open to collaboration from others,
  or something you want to learn together.
* **OR** if you're fresh out of ideas, come with a willingness to help out a
  stranger with theirs!

What to expect:
* 11:00am - 11:30am: gathering and chit-chat
* 11:30am - 12:00pm: explain projects, form groups, set up workstations
* 12:00pm - 05:30pm: work on stuff together
* 05:30pm - 06:00pm: show others what you built and what you learned

Since we're meeting at a restaurant that can serve us food where we're working, you will
be able to just take a break and order lunch whenever you're hungry.

[**PLEASE RSVP ON LUMA**](https://luma.com/i7rfzqoa) so that we can appropriately plan
for the number of guests.
